  "group": "Obsidian",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "noteIntro",
      "type": "NoteNode",
      "x": 1150,
      "y": 1035,
      "init": {
        "label": "Write it back to Obsidian",
        "body": "# Your vault as a table\n\n**Vault Folder** reads a folder of notes as one table: a row per note, a column per frontmatter key, with lists and sub-tables kept in the cells. Filter keeps the notes whose tags contain `book`; Sort orders them by rating.\n\nThe second chain writes back. Read the project notes, add a **health** label from status and priority, and **Write to Obsidian** puts it on each note as a property; a Bases view over the folder then shows the new column. It loads disarmed and previews every change, so nothing is written until you press Run.\n\nWith no vault folder set in Settings, the readers use the bundled sample vault (which refuses writes); point them at your own to write for real.",
        "color": "violet",
        "width": 380,
        "height": 260
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "health",
      "type": "ComputedColumnNode",
      "x": 2798,
      "y": 1391,
      "init": {
        "label": "health from status + priority",
        "expr": "IF(@status=\"done\",\"done\",IF(@status=\"blocked\",\"at risk\",IF(@priority>=4,\"push\",\"steady\")))",
        "addAs": "text"
      },
      "stringLiterals": {
        "name": "health",
        "after": ""
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "write",
      "type": "WriteObsidianNode",
      "x": 3145,
      "y": 1391,
      "init": {
        "label": "Write to Obsidian",
        "target": "properties",
        "addMissing": true,
        "writeBase": false
      },
      "stringLiterals": {
        "keys": "health"
      }
    },
